-# Chronyx Mobile 0.3.0-alpha.3
+# Chronyx Mobile 0.4.0-alpha.4
 
 Native Android browser shell derived from the verified Chronyx Desktop 0.7.0-alpha.37 product/security baseline. Android does not run the Electron desktop architecture; this build intentionally uses the device's updatable Chromium-based Android WebView instead of emulating or exposing Electron APIs.
 
@@ -41,3 +41,7 @@
 Starting with 0.3.0-alpha.3, distributable APKs are signed with the persistent Chronyx Mobile release certificate rather than an ephemeral CI debug key. Future updates must keep the same applicationId (`com.chronyx.browser.mobile`), use a higher versionCode, and be signed by the same release key.
 
 Release certificate SHA-256: `08:E3:DF:D2:CC:CA:DD:A1:EC:1F:6E:8C:97:14:B4:76:F4:D8:98:0C:70:FC:7A:D8:20:7F:22:75:CF:41:6E:A9`.
+
+
+### ChatGPT compatibility
+Chronyx Mobile can automatically enable a compatibility profile for ChatGPT/OpenAI tabs: standard mobile WebView UA, DOM storage, cookies including third-party cookies for that tab, media playback suitable for voice/WebRTC flows, popup support through user gestures, Android file chooser, camera/microphone permissions, download cookies, and persistent cookie flushing. Authentication/security challenges are never bypassed; a default-browser fallback is available because OpenAI recommends Chrome or Brave for Android login flows.
